    "rich_text_8atpqp": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_7jTBtL": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<strong>Serving Freeze Dried Salmon Dog Treats: How Much Is Too Much?</strong>",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_cE7LyU": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Moderation is key when it comes to feeding freeze dried salmon dog treats. These treats should make up no more than 10% of your dog’s daily caloric intake. Small dogs may only need one or two treats, while larger dogs might enjoy a few more. If your dog prefers softer treats, you can rehydrate the freeze dried salmon with a little warm water to give it a meatier texture<br/></p>"
          }
        }
      },
